    "question": {
      ":question/id": "6eb081a1-755d-59ed-a965-859c3dddcfd8",
      ":question/problem": "Let\n$A=\\begin{bmatrix}-4 & -3 \\\\ -2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{bmatrix}$\nand\n$B=\\begin{bmatrix}-4 & -3 & -2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & 3\\end{bmatrix}.$\nWhat are the dimensions of $BA?$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "We notice that $A$ is a $4\\times 2$ matrix and $B$ is a $2\\times 4$ matrix. \n\nThere are $4$ columns in $B$ and $4$ rows in $A.$ Since the number of columns in $B$ equals the number of rows in $A,$ the matrices $B$ and $A$ are conformable for multiplication. \n\nThe product $BA$ has dimensions $2\\times 2:$\n\n$$\n{B}_{2\\times \\boxed{\\text{4}}}{\\times }_{\u2713}{A}_{\\boxed{\\text{4}}\\times 2}={BA}_{2\\times 2}\n$$",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/hard",
